{"kind":"assert","text":"Disposition on `a8d20fcc`: the allowlist stays as it is, as you\nsay. The Node run before START found this in 2 minutes, and a gate\nwould have found it in 30.\n\nThe layer assertion is right, and the repair follows it:\n\n1. A Derive test imports nothing from `dap-git`. The fixture helper\n   takes the bound as an argument and holds no import of the\n   ceiling.\n2. The owner in the layer that owns the ceiling passes the shared\n   value to the helper. The Derive corpus passes a bound of its\n   own, and its test states a property of the graph at a bound. It\n   does not state the value of the archive ceiling.\n3. If Derive source, and not only a test, enforces this same\n   ceiling, the definition is in the wrong layer. Then stop and\n   tell me, and I rule on a move of the definition to the lowest\n   layer that enforces it.\n\nThen the whole Node stage again, and START 3 with the hit list and\nthe owner counts of `a1c5a189`.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}